    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">The Max 3/8-Inch Variance Rule for Risers and Treads</h2>
    <p>
      Under IRC Section R311.7.5.3, the tolerance for stair construction is strict: <strong>the greatest riser height within any flight of stairs shall not exceed the smallest by more than 3/8-inch (0.375 inch)</strong>. The human brain creates a rhythmic motor pattern when walking up or down stairs; a sudden height discrepancy of even 1/2-inch causes the foot to catch the tread nosing, causing violent falls.
    </p>
  </div>

