      trade="Structural Deck Engineering"
      content="Stair stringers must be cut from a single continuous piece of lumber from top header to bottom concrete landing pad. You cannot splice or sister two pieces together with plywood gussets or metal ties to achieve length. If your total run exceeds the length of standard 16-foot 2x12s, building code requires an intermediate level landing platform (minimum 36-in x 36-in) with dedicated post footers."
    />
